 1 file changed, 158 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md

diff --git a/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4eff9e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+# Why CVE-2025-1371 in `elfutils` 0.188 is a False Positive
+
+## Overview: What Is CVE-2025-1371?
+
+CVE-2025-1371 is a null pointer dereference vulnerability in the `handle_dynamic_symtab` function of the `readelf.c` component in GNU elfutils. The vulnerability occurs when processing corrupt ELF files with broken program headers, where `gelf_getphdr` returns NULL but the code attempts to dereference the pointer without checking.
+
+According to the CVE description, this vulnerability affects GNU elfutils version 0.192. The patch is identified as commit `b38e562a4c907e08171c76b8b2def8464d5a104a`.
+
+---
+
+## Why CVE-2025-1371 is a False Positive for Version 0.188
+
+Security scanners may flag **CVE-2025-1371** in images using elfutils 0.188, but:
+
+- **The vulnerable function `handle_dynamic_symtab` does NOT exist in version 0.188**
+- This function was introduced in a later version (0.189+) after version 0.188 was released
+- Version 0.188 was released on **November 2, 2022** (commit `e9f3045c`)
+- The function `handle_dynamic_symtab` was introduced on **March 27, 2023** (commit `4d8de4b2`)
+- Therefore, version 0.188 **cannot be affected** by this vulnerability
+
+---
+
+## CVE Breakdown
+
+---
+
+## CVE-2025-1371 – Null Pointer Dereference in `handle_dynamic_symtab`
+
+- **Component:** `readelf.c` (eu-read component)
+- **Function:** `handle_dynamic_symtab`
+- **Issue:** When processing corrupt ELF files with broken program headers, `gelf_getphdr` may return NULL, but the code attempts to access `phdr->p_type` without checking for NULL first
+- **Impact:** Null pointer dereference → may cause:
+  - Crashes when processing malformed ELF files
+  - Denial of service
+  - Potential for exploitation if combined with other vulnerabilities
+- **Root Cause:** Missing NULL check before dereferencing `phdr` pointer
+- **Upstream Status:** 🛠️ **Fixed** in commit `b38e562a4c907e08171c76b8b2def8464d5a104a`  
+  → [Sourceware Bug #32655](https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=32655)
+
+---
+
+## Version Timeline Analysis
+
+| Version | Release Date | Contains `handle_dynamic_symtab`? | Status |
+|---------|--------------|-----------------------------------|--------|
+| 0.188   | 2022-11-02   | ❌ **NO** (0 occurrences)        | ✅ **NOT VULNERABLE** |
+| 0.189   | 2023-03-03   | ✅ Yes (introduced in commit `4d8de4b2` on 2023-03-27) | ⚠️ Potentially vulnerable |
+| 0.190   | 2023-11-03   | ✅ Yes                             | ⚠️ Potentially vulnerable |
+| 0.191   | 2024-03-01   | ✅ Yes                             | ⚠️ Potentially vulnerable |
+| 0.192   | 2024-10-18   | ✅ Yes                             | ⚠️ Vulnerable (fixed in later commit) |
+
+---
+
+## Technical Evidence
+
+### Code Analysis
+
+**Version 0.188 (commit `e9f3045c`):**
+```bash
+$ git show e9f3045c:src/readelf.c | grep -c "handle_dynamic_symtab"
+0
+```
+Result: **Function does not exist** in version 0.188
+
+**Version with function (commit `4d8de4b2`):**
+```bash
+$ git show 4d8de4b2:src/readelf.c | grep -c "handle_dynamic_symtab"
+3
+```
+Result: **Function introduced** in commit `4d8de4b2` (March 27, 2023)
+
+### Vulnerable Code Pattern (Before Fix)
+
+The vulnerable code in versions 0.189-0.192 (before the fix):
+
+```c
+static bool
+handle_dynamic_symtab (Ebl *ebl)
+{
+  GElf_Phdr phdr_mem;
+  GElf_Phdr *phdr = NULL;
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < phnum; ++i)
+    {
+      phdr = gelf_getphdr (ebl->elf, i, &phdr_mem);
+      if (phdr->p_type == PT_DYNAMIC)  // ❌ VULNERABLE: No NULL check
+        break;
+    }
+  // ...
+}
+```
+
+### Fixed Code Pattern (After Fix)
+
+The fixed code in commit `b38e562a4c907e08171c76b8b2def8464d5a104a`:
+
+```c
+static bool
+handle_dynamic_symtab (Ebl *ebl)
+{
+  GElf_Phdr phdr_mem;
+  GElf_Phdr *phdr = NULL;
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < phnum; ++i)
+    {
+      phdr = gelf_getphdr (ebl->elf, i, &phdr_mem);
+      if (phdr == NULL || phdr->p_type == PT_DYNAMIC)  // ✅ FIXED: NULL check added
+        break;
+    }
+  // ...
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## Why This Is a False Positive for Version 0.188
+
+1. **Function Non-Existence:** The vulnerable function `handle_dynamic_symtab` was not present in version 0.188. It was added in a later version (0.189+) as part of a feature to display dynamic symbol tables without section headers.
+
+2. **Timeline Evidence:**
+   - Version 0.188 released: **November 2, 2022**
+   - Function introduced: **March 27, 2023** (commit `4d8de4b2`)
+   - Time gap: **~5 months** between 0.188 release and function introduction
+
+3. **Code Verification:**
+   - Searching for `handle_dynamic_symtab` in version 0.188 returns **0 matches**
+   - The function only appears in versions 0.189 and later
+
+4. **CVE Scope:** The CVE description explicitly mentions version 0.192, which aligns with the timeline where the function exists.
+
+---
+
+## Recommended Actions
+
+| Scenario | Action |
+|----------|--------|
+| Using elfutils 0.188 | ✅ **No action required** - This is a false positive. The vulnerability does not affect this version. |
+| Using elfutils 0.189-0.192 | ⚠️ **Update required** - Apply the fix from commit `b38e562a4c907e08171c76b8b2def8464d5a104a` or upgrade to a patched version |
+| Using elfutils > 0.192 | ✅ **Check patch status** - Verify that the fix has been applied in your version |
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+- CVE-2025-1371 affects the `handle_dynamic_symtab` function in `readelf.c`
+- The function **does not exist** in elfutils version 0.188
+- Version 0.188 was released **before** the function was introduced
+- This CVE is a **false positive** for version 0.188
+- Security scanners flagging this CVE for version 0.188 should be marked as false positives
+
+---
+
+## References
+
+- [CVE-2025-1371](https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2025-1371)
+- [Sourceware Bug #32655](https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=32655)
+- [Fix Commit: b38e562a4c907e08171c76b8b2def8464d5a104a](https://sourceware.org/git/?p=elfutils.git;a=commit;h=b38e562a4c907e08171c76b8b2def8464d5a104a)
+- [Function Introduction: 4d8de4b2](https://sourceware.org/git/?p=elfutils.git;a=commit;h=4d8de4b2)
+- [elfutils Git Repository](https://sourceware.org/git/?p=elfutils.git)
+
